======================================================================
Optional Git and SSH setup
======================================================================

To enable the bundled SSH aliases and Git defaults together, run:

  remote-ssh setup

For granular setup, run:

  remote-ssh ssh setup
  remote-ssh git setup

`remote-ssh ssh setup` creates `dots/ssh/config.local` from the example if
needed and adds it to `$HOME/.ssh/config` via `Include`.

`remote-ssh git setup` creates `dots/git/user.local` from the example if needed
and adds the base config via `git config --global include.path ...`.

In remote-ssh shells, `dots/git/user.local` is also applied as a session Git
identity override. This affects Git commands in that SSH session without
writing to repository `.git/config` files.

Edit `dots/git/user.local` and `dots/ssh/config.local`, then point repository
remotes at the alias:

  git remote set-url origin git@github.com-myuser:OWNER/REPO.git
